{
  "id": "1b6f739f-8774-4da2-af4f-5f88d0514507",
  "featureId": "cd083ad1-8310-4368-981b-d14c73c20d96",
  "number": 91,
  "shortId": "DUEHY",
  "priority": 12,
  "slug": "gridui-11-text-fits-its-box-label-truncation-and-item-s-second-line",
  "title": "gridui-11: Text fits its box — Label truncation and Item's second line",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "The library's missing text capability, recorded as an open gap in AGENTS for months and worked around four separate times.",
  "description": "Two small widget capabilities that four call sites have been hand-rolling because the library never had them.\n\n## Why it exists\n\nAGENTS.md records it plainly: *\"truncation/ellipsis + wrapping (a long label overflows its box today)\"* — in a **prose list of open gaps, never filed as a task**, which is precisely how it stayed open while four hand-written truncations grew around it:\n\n- `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:286` `truncate_path_left` (start-ellipsis, keeps the tail — paths);\n- `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:391` the pane info bar's overflow budget, measuring with its own `char_w = font * 0.6` (a hand-copy of `MONO_ADVANCE_RATIO`);\n- `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:1428` `truncate_sidebar_git_branch` (a fixed char cap);\n- the command palette's `fit()` (F003/P085/T358).\n\n`heca/src/providers/workspaces/mod.rs:1231` even carries a comment deferring to *\"when label truncation/wrapping is settled\"*.\n\n## What already exists — nothing new is needed underneath\n\n- `Label::remeasure` sizes itself `chars × font × MONO_ADVANCE_RATIO` wide and `font × MONO_LINE_RATIO` tall, and `paint` draws into `base.bounds`. Fitting to the box is therefore a paint-time cut against the same measure the layout used.\n- `Layout::flex_shrink` and `min_size` exist (taffy 0.7), and `style.rs:423` documents `Px(0.0)` as the way to let a node go below its content size — so \"may be given less than its natural width\" needs no engine change.\n- `Item` **already composes**: its label is a real `Label` child (index 1) between two slot `Flex`es, and its own doc says the label \"can be swapped or extended without touching `Item::paint`\". The second line is another `Label`, never text drawn by `Item`.\n\n## Scope\n\n`Label` gains truncation (End and Start ellipsis) and `Item` gains a description line. **Both stay in `heca-grid-ui`** — a widget is what can be built there, and these can. The four app-side copies are deleted by F011/P089/T376, which is blocked on this.\n\n## Behaviors to preserve\n\nExisting labels are unaffected unless they opt in — a `Label` with no truncation set keeps its current natural size and overflow behaviour, or every layout in the app shifts at once. `Item`'s row height only changes when a description is present. Measure stays the shared `MONO_ADVANCE_RATIO` (a Phase-A approximation until cosmic-text shaping lands — centralising it here is what makes that a one-place fix later).",
  "notes": "",
  "goals": [],
