    {
      "id": "3019641b-6df6-4f5f-b3fe-e1c54c490117",
      "phaseId": "1b6f739f-8774-4da2-af4f-5f88d0514507",
      "number": 380,
      "shortId": "29F9C",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "item-gains-a-description-line",
      "title": "Item gains a description line — a second Label, not painted text",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "The row's second line, composed the way the row already composes its first.\n\n## What exists\n\n`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/item.rs` builds three children in `Item::new` (:117-122) and names their indices:\n\n```\nconst LEADING: usize = 0;   // Flex::empty() slot\n// 1 = the label — `Label::new(label).align(TextAlign::Start).grow(1.0)`\nconst TRAILING: usize = 2;  // Flex::empty() slot\n```\n\nwith the doc: *\"The label is a real `Label` child (not text drawn by `Item`), so the row is composed like every other widget: the engine lays the three out, each paints itself, and the label can be swapped or extended **without touching `Item::paint`**.\"* That is the seam this task uses — the description is another `Label`, and `Item::paint` is not touched.\n\nConstants that will need to follow the row's height: `ROW_H` (38.0), `FONT_SIZE` (15.0), the selection pill inset `SEL_INSET`, the active bar `ACTIVE_BAR_FRAC`.\n\n## What to build\n\n`Item::description(text)`: the label child becomes a `Flex::column` of the title `Label` and a muted description `Label` (theme `muted`, smaller `font_scale`), and the row grows to two lines **only when a description is set**. Slots stay vertically centred against the whole row; the active bar and the selection pill scale with the row rather than assuming `ROW_H`.\n\nPair it with `Label::truncate` (T379) so a long description cuts instead of overflowing — the palette rows are the first consumer, via F011.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **No description ⇒ nothing changes**: same height, same paint, same measure. Every existing `Item` in the sidebar, menus and `Select` options must be pixel-identical.\n- `label_signal()` keeps addressing the **title**; a description signal is separate if one is needed later (not now — no consumer).\n- The description must not steal the row's activation: it is a plain child, and `on_activate` stays the row's.\n\n## Test\n\nBuild an `Item` with and without a description, run `LayoutEngine`, and assert: the two-line row is taller than the one-line row by one line; both labels are children of the label column with the description **below** the title and left-aligned to it; the leading/trailing slots stay centred; a description-less `Item` measures exactly as it does today (guard against a silent global row-height change).",
