    {
      "id": "5408f2d8-b2fa-47dd-867e-e4d5cbf1964d",
      "phaseId": "1b6f739f-8774-4da2-af4f-5f88d0514507",
      "number": 382,
      "shortId": "73MPT",
      "priority": 3,
      "shortName": "label-wraps-height-from-width",
      "title": "Label wraps — height from width, the other half of the gap",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "The second half of AGENTS.md's open gap (*\"truncation/ellipsis **+ wrapping**\"*). `Label::truncate` (T379) closed the first half; this is the harder one.\n\n## Why it is harder than truncation\n\nTruncation is a **paint-time** cut against the box the engine already gave the label — the measure never changes. Wrapping changes the measure itself: a wrapped label's **height depends on its resolved width**, which a fixed `Length::Px` measure cannot express.\n\n`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/label.rs::remeasure` today sets:\n\n```\nwidth  = chars × font × MONO_ADVANCE_RATIO      // one line, natural width\nheight = font × MONO_LINE_RATIO                 // exactly one line\n```\n\nTaffy (0.7, `heca-grid-ui/src/layout.rs`) supports content-driven sizing through a **measure function** on leaf nodes — that path is what this task has to reach; the engine does not use it for labels today. Check whether `LayoutEngine` already wires one for any widget before adding a second mechanism.\n\n## What to build\n\n`Label::wrap(bool)` (or `Wrap::{None, Word}`) — mutually exclusive with `truncate`, since a label either cuts or reflows:\n- break on **word** boundaries, falling back to a hard break for a word longer than the line;\n- height = `lines × font × MONO_LINE_RATIO`, computed from the width the engine offers;\n- the run rect / decorations follow the **last** line, or span each line, whichever the existing `run_rect` contract can honour — decide and document it.\n\n## The consumer that asked for it (2026-07-30)\n\nThe command palette wraps **the selected row's description only**, and the list **reflows** — rows below shift down as the cursor moves, CSS-style, which the maintainer chose explicitly over a fixed two-line allowance. So the palette needs per-row heights that change with selection; row geometry there is already per-row (`row_rects`), so the reflow follows from the label's height being honest.\n\n## Behaviors to preserve\n\nA label that sets neither `wrap` nor `truncate` keeps today's single-line measure exactly — every existing layout in the app depends on it. Wrapping must not silently change the natural width either: a wrapped label still asks for its full width and only *accepts* less.\n\n## Test\n\nAssert the drawn lines, not a flag: the same text in a wide box paints one text run, in a narrow box paints N runs at increasing y, and the label's measured height is N line-heights. A long unbreakable word still fits (hard break) rather than overflowing.",
