    {
      "id": "7dae47ea-461b-49be-b1ad-517005312d80",
      "phaseId": "1b6f739f-8774-4da2-af4f-5f88d0514507",
      "number": 383,
      "shortId": "GCCMN",
      "priority": 4,
      "shortName": "the-palette-keeps-a-margin-bel",
      "title": "The palette keeps a margin below it — the vertical counterpart of PANEL_VIEWPORT_FRAC",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "🔴 Reported in the app on 2026-07-30, right after the height fix (`7475a81`): **the palette panel touches the very bottom of the window.**\n\n## Why\n\n`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/command_palette.rs:325` — `visible_rows` fills the list down to\n\n```rust\nlet mut room = (vp.h * (1.0 - TOP_FRAC) - chrome).max(0.0);\n```\n\nand `layout()` (:445) places the panel at `py = vh * TOP_FRAC` (:486) with `panel_h = PAD + query_h + PAD + list_h + PAD` (:479). `chrome` is exactly that non-list part, so the bound resolves to\n\n    panel_bottom ≤ vh * TOP_FRAC + vh * (1 - TOP_FRAC) = vh\n\n— the window's bottom edge, to the pixel. Nothing reserves room **below** the panel, so on a short window the last row sits flush against the screen edge.\n\nThe horizontal axis already has this: `PANEL_VIEWPORT_FRAC = 0.92` (:97) caps the panel at 92% of the window width, leaving 4% clear on each side. The vertical axis has no equivalent — `TOP_FRAC` (:99) is an offset, not a margin, and it only guards the top.\n\n## What to build\n\nA `BOTTOM_FRAC` constant beside `TOP_FRAC`, documented as the vertical counterpart of the side gap `PANEL_VIEWPORT_FRAC` leaves: `(1.0 - 0.92) / 2.0 = 0.04` of the viewport, so the gap under the panel matches the gap beside it as a fraction of its own axis. Subtract it in `visible_rows`:\n\n```rust\nlet mut room = (vp.h * (1.0 - TOP_FRAC - BOTTOM_FRAC) - chrome).max(0.0);\n```\n\nOne place only — `layout()` derives `panel_h` from the rows `visible_rows` admitted, so the panel shrinks with it and no second clamp is needed.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **The gap is quantised by the row height.** A row is two lines (described list) or taller (stacked bindings), so dropping one row can leave far more than 4% clear. That is the floor being a floor, not a target — do not try to distribute the remainder.\n- **The one-row floor still wins** (:344): a window too short for even a single row keeps showing one clipped row rather than an empty panel, and that row may still reach past the margin. Keep that behaviour and keep the test viewports above it.\n- **Non-finite viewport** (:328) returns early, before any of this — unchanged.\n\n## Test\n\nExtend `the_palette_never_runs_off_a_short_window` (`heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs:3701`). It asserts `bottom <= viewport.h + 0.5` today, which the flush panel passes — that is why the bug shipped. Assert a **gap**: `bottom <= viewport.h * (1.0 - 0.04) + 0.5`, at the three viewports it already sweeps (1280x900, 1280x480, 900x320), with the failure message reporting the measured gap.\n\nVisual verification is the user's — a test can prove the number, not that it looks like breathing room.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDone — verified visually by the user 2026-08-03 (\"the height of the command palette is perfect\"). `BOTTOM_FRAC = 0.08` added beside `TOP_FRAC` in heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/command_palette.rs; `visible_rows` fills to `vp.h * (1.0 - TOP_FRAC - BOTTOM_FRAC)`. One place only — `layout()` derives `panel_h` from the rows `visible_rows` admitted.\n\nTwo things worth carrying:\n1. **4% was not enough.** Deriving the margin from `PANEL_VIEWPORT_FRAC`'s side gap ((1-0.92)/2) was tried first and still read as touching: the panel's bottom edge landed on the top of the bottom pane, so the gap vanished into a boundary that was already there. 0.08 is a measured-by-eye value, not a derived one.\n2. **The test passed against the bug even after being rewritten to assert a gap.** Its three sampled viewports left 23px–69px of slack because the gap is quantised by row height and only collapses where the room divides evenly into rows. It now sweeps heights 260..=1000 at two widths; against the unfixed code it fails at 1280x270 with 0.6px of room. Sampling a geometry bound is not testing it.\n\nNot yet committed — awaiting the user's word.",
      "notes": "",
